{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Fix landed. Gerrit change 2011 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2011), LLM-Review +1 (rebar review bot) + Verified +1 (rebar CI bot, run 32512417349, full matrix green), submitted and MERGED as 4fbeb05607 on main (server-side rebase over 2563919111).\n\nWhat landed: rebar.toml [llm] pins bedrock_region_name = \"us-east-1\" (per the operator ruling above — the project's measured region) beside the region-scoped us.* model pins; docs/config.md documents the key and the pin-the-region-beside-region-scoped-model-pins guidance; tests/unit/test_bedrock_provider.py pins (a) an AWS_PROFILE-only shell (no REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION / AWS_DEFAULT_REGION / AWS_REGION) resolving the region from the discovered rebar.toml table and it reaching the boto3 session explicitly, (b) REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION keeping precedence over the table value, and (c) a repo guard that this checkout pins the region beside its region-scoped model pins (seen RED before the config edit, GREEN after).\n\nOriginal report replicated as resolved: in the fix worktree, env -u REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION -u AWS_DEFAULT_REGION -u AWS_REGION AWS_PROFILE=frontier → LLMConfig.from_env().bedrock_region_name == 'us-east-1'.\n\nAC status: AC1 met (us-east-1 per ruling); AC2 met (profile-only shell resolves; pinned by test at the config seam); AC3 met (existing precedence preserved, now pinned by test); AC4 amended per ruling → follow-up task astatine-pixilated-shrimp (cda8-0f27-b324-4446), linked discovered_from. Closing."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787338888044439001,"uuid":"02b4f0cb-4dcd-42e6-bf1e-0e76c429d9ea"}